    "notes": "Actual root Codex/0S workspace instructions.",
    "inlineText": "# Repo MCP Rule Summary\n\nMounted 0S apps use the shared FS27/SkyGate/Free99 owner lane owned by the main Worker.\nDo not create a separate app-owned credential lane for mounted surfaces.\nOwner surfaces forward the shared gate session through the Worker helpers and accepted session headers.\nMounted API routes rely on requireGateAuth, requireOperatorAuth, and shared owner-session helpers.\nNew 0S surfaces must pass through enforceZeroOsGate before assets or proxied APIs.\nPublic metadata stays tiny: favicon, robots, sitemap, and the owner login/introspection entrypoints.\n\nMCP source of truth: quantumskyes from .mcp.json using MCP/stdio-server.mjs.\nDefault workflow: run npm run mcp:mine -- <target-folder>, read the receipt, apply changes, rerun mining, then deploy/prove the same target.",
